  <section>
    <h2>What Canapalandia is today</h2>
    <p>Canapalandia is an online editorial project covering industrial hemp, CBD, cannabis light, regulation, research, sustainability and culture. The site is not a shop and does not manage sales, orders or payments for hemp-based products.</p>
    <p>Our aim is to turn topics that are often technical or controversial into more readable content, distinguishing, as far as possible, facts, sources, interpretations and opinions.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Where we come from</h2>
    <p>The project began in 2016 as a blog dedicated to hemp. Over the years it has gone through different phases, including a previous commercial experience. Today Canapalandia has returned to its main purpose: informing, explaining and creating useful tools for people who want to understand this world better.</p>
    <p class="institutional-note">Some older pages and articles belong to the history of the project and are progressively updated when they no longer represent the current Canapalandia.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How we work</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We prefer primary sources, official documents and scientific studies when available.</li>
      <li>We state dates and context when a rule, study or news story may change over time.</li>
      <li>We separate editorial content from commercial collaborations.</li>
      <li>We correct articles when errors or more up-to-date information emerge.</li>
      <li>We do not present content as medical or legal advice.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To report an error or propose a correction, use the <a href="/en/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Independence and sustainability of the project</h2>
    <p>Canapalandia may be supported through advertising, sponsored content, collaborations, affiliate links and voluntary reader contributions. When content results from a commercial collaboration, our aim is to make that relationship recognisable and keep it separate from ordinary editorial work.</p>
    <p>A commercial relationship should not determine the conclusions of an informational article. For collaborations and advertising, see <a href="/en/advertising/">Advertising and collaborations</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Tools, not verdicts</h2>
    <p>Alongside articles, we develop small free tools. For example, <a href="/en/lab/">Canapalandia Lab</a> helps readers interpret selected data found in COA certificates. These tools are intended to help users orient themselves: they do not certify the legality, safety, quality or suitability for consumption of a product.</p>
    <p>For limits on the use of the site's content, see the <a href="/en/disclaimer/">Legal Disclaimer</a>.</p>
  </section>
